      "report": "# Cut notes: A Video Is a Program\n\n**Planning speed:** tester's mean 675.5 ms per frame x 1.25 = **844.375 ms per frame** (the 2451 ms largest is the cold first frame).\n\nWhole film at P: 720 frames x 844.375 ms = 608.0 s (under 45 min): sheet fps 60 kept.\n\n**Piece length L:** 5.4 s = 9 beats of 0.6 s (bpm 100), 324 frames, 273.6 s at P (limit 300 s). The next whole beat count (6.0 s, 360 frames) would take 304.0 s.\n\n## Video pieces (cards, each the page with data-offset = start on its <html> tag)\n| Piece | Start (s) | Length (s) | Frames | Est. render at P (s) | Card bytes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| p1 | 0.0 | 5.4 | 324 | 273.6 | 44044 |\n| p2 | 5.4 | 5.4 | 324 | 273.6 | 44046 |\n| p3 | 10.8 | 1.2 | 72 | 60.8 | 44047 |\n\nTotal: 12.0 s, 720 frames = 12 s x 60 fps. No transitions, no \"at\".\n\n## Sound item\n`score`: the page exactly as supplied (no data-offset), 12 s, at 0, no fades; the edit node records its window.renderAudio for the whole film.\n\n## Output\n1080 x 1350, 60 fps, crf 18, -16 LUFS, true peak -1 dB, a still every 4 s.\n\n## Checks run in cut.py (all passed)\n- every card at most 262,144 bytes; 3 cards (max 40), 12.0 s of cards (max 120 s)\n- timeline.json: **185039 bytes** (max 1,900,000)\n- pieces' frames add up to length x fps (720)\n",
