  "note": "Run on the live AwwO, in the operator’s own account and workspace, on 2026-10-26, every agent on Claude Opus 5.5 working in its own sandbox computer. The film answers an Opus 5.5 video prompt by Karmi (x.com/0xKarmi/status/2108495927988129839, prompt 12286 of YouMind’s Opus 5.5 collection), which drew its rule as an X-ray butterfly: the model writes a drawing program, not a video file, and each picture depends on its frame number alone. AwwO renders pages the same way, and this film shows it with AwwO’s own rules. The canvas’s text was written for this film by the operator beforehand: the Director’s task (the prompt adapted to AwwO, with the facts the film may state and the look), the kernel contract every module writes to, each builder’s duty, and the tester’s and the editor’s tasks. What is seen and heard is what the canvas’s agents wrote. The canvas ran three times, each run after the first running only the nodes it named, on the kept outputs of the rest. In the first (10:59 to 11:27 UTC) the three scene modules and the sound started 5 minutes after the kernel, their first start having found every sandbox computer busy (six canvases were running at once), and everything finished but the edit, whose first piece never rendered: the X-ray module made the page wait for a timer before it was ready, and AwwO’s renderer runs no timer until a frame is drawn, so the page never became ready. The tester had timed the frames with the page’s timers running and could not see it. In the second (12:05 to 12:12) the tester ran again with a task that times the frames with the timers stopped, as the renderer does: it found that the page never became ready, traced it to that wait and changed it to a promise that needs no timer; and the editor cut the checked page into three pieces (5.4, 5.4 and 1.2 s). The third (12:18 to 12:21) ran the edit, which rendered each piece from the page and recorded the page’s own sound (window.renderAudio), with no model. The tester found 12 of the page’s 12 tests passing and all 4 planted failures caught, before its fix and after it. The canvas’s Review node ran beside the edit and is not part of this case.",
